        "call": "Fetch https://fns-prod.azureedge.us/sites/default/files/resource-files/37wic-monthly-9.pdf through the official WIC Data Tables page.",
        "result": "National Total Participants: October 2025 6,909,938; November 6,771,734; December 6,712,611; January 2026 6,696,300; February 6,664,741; March 6,703,035; April 6,708,518; May 6,687,977; June 6,669,554. FY2026 figures are preliminary and subject to revision."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Read historical June and August national Total Participants from the same official monthly PDF.",
        "result": "June/August counts were 6,732,424/6,722,170 in 2023, 6,736,885/6,830,287 in 2024, and 6,883,200/6,911,108 in 2025."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The outside-view base rate is persistence from June, with a seasonal adjustment estimated from the three fetched June-to-August comparisons. Their changes are -10,254, +93,402, and +27,908 participants, averaging +37,018.667 participants. This gives a seasonal persistence prior of 6.706572667 million."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Fetch archived January, February, and April 2026 Keydata PDFs listed in sourceContext and read each report's latest-month participation value in Table 21.",
        "result": "January's archived count was 6,689,525 versus the current 6,696,300; February's was 6,640,819 versus 6,664,741; April's was 6,704,900 versus 6,708,518. Subsequent upward revisions were 6,775, 23,922, and 3,618 participants. These archives are initial-month vintage proxies; their chronology against the first publication of the separate national monthly table was not certified."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Fetch https://fns-prod.azureedge.us/wic/fr-042926 for the income eligibility mechanism applying during the target month.",
        "result": "Guidelines effective July 1, 2026 retain the maximum income criterion of 185% of poverty. For a four-person household in the contiguous-state schedule, the maximum is $61,050 annually or $5,088 monthly."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level: June anchors the forecast at 6.669554 million. Momentum: April-to-June participation fell by 38,964 people; extrapolating half that two-month decline subtracts 0.019482 million. Reporting mechanism: the three archived-to-current revisions average 0.011438333 million, which is subtracted as a small early-vintage proxy adjustment. Policy: the annual July eligibility update could support enrollment, but no fetched enrollment response identifies a separate numerical effect; routine summer effects remain in the seasonal adjustment. No additional one-off adjustment is quantified."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use seasonal persistence with damped recent momentum and an early-vintage proxy correction. The historical sample is nine monthly levels from October 2025 through June 2026, plus three June-to-August seasonal comparisons and three archived revision pairs. Point = 6.669554 + 0.037018667 - 0.019482 - 0.011438333 = 6.675652333 million. Across the eight successive monthly changes, sigma = 0.051951446 million. The normal-approximation one-month half-width is 1.28*sigma = 0.066497850 million; multiplying by sqrt(2) for the two-month horizon gives 0.094042162 million. Final rounded bounds are 6.581610 and 6.769694 million. This is a model-based 80% interval; the small archive sample does not establish complete first-print error calibration."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Successive changes in persons are [-138204, -59123, -16311, -31559, 38294, 5483, -20541, -18423], with mean -30048. Sample sigma = sqrt(sum((change + 30048)^2)/7)/1000000 = 0.051951446. Momentum adjustment = 0.5*2*((6.669554 - 6.708518)/2) = -0.019482. Vintage adjustment = -(6775 + 23922 + 3618)/3/1000000 = -0.011438333. Unrounded interval = 6.675652333 +/- 0.094042162 = [6.581610172, 6.769694495]; round to six decimal places in millions."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Ledger discrepancies: the fetched monthly table reports persons, so the registered multiplication factor 0.001 would be incorrect unless its input were first converted to thousands. This forecast preserves the registered unit and converts persons directly to millions. USDA's official April 30, 2026 announcement identifies the Food and Nutrition Administration as formerly FNS; current pages and documents were accessed through its official hosting mirror. The registered allowlist contains only www.fns.usda.gov, so current hosting may require resolver metadata review. The target identifier and registered resolution URL remain unchanged."
